The Switch node's output ports aren't being auto-declared from the `handleConfiguration` I provided in the definition — the validator is checking handle declarations and doesn't see `case-p1` or `case-p2` as declared handles. 

Looking at the Switch node definition I wrote, I declared handles statically:
```json
"handleConfiguration": [
  ...
  {
    "position": "right",
    "handles": [
      {
        "id": "default",
        "label": "Default",
        "type": "source",
        "handleType": "output"
      }
    ]
  }
]
```

But the `case-p1` and `case-p2` ports are dynamic — they're generated based on the `cases` input. The real Switch definition from the registry likely has a special mechanism for generating handles dynamically from the input array, so I need to check what that looks like.

